      {
        "id": 244887,
        "name": "Cat that lives with Guise",
        "username": "Guise-Cat",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/guise-cat/{size}/5169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2022-04-30T01:05:29.267Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group quote-modified\" data-username=\"skywhale\" data-post=\"24\" data-topic=\"29275\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/skywhale/48/5248_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> skywhale:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group quote-modified\" data-username=\"X-metal\" data-post=\"23\" data-topic=\"29275\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/x-metal/48/4892_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> X-metal:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Demon Cat (is it one word or two) is wrong, they actually wrote about Demons at both the start of the month and the end of the month as all cats are demons, which I suppose makes their name ironic.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p><a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/guise-cat\">@Guise-Cat</a>, are you just gonna take this slander?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Slander? More like a compliment. You think these claws are just for show? <em>&gt;shinkt&lt;</em></p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"OddballPaladin\" data-post=\"29\" data-topic=\"29275\" data-full=\"true\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/o/d26b3c/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> OddballPaladin:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Nah, that’s just how cats normally look. Remember, they’re only somewhat domesticated killing machines (which is why cats should be indoor only… otherwise many species of birds and ground mammals may become endangered). Guise-Cat sounds a lot like a few that I’ve known. Like my Dad’s cat that will only let him or my step-mother pet her, and anyone else will get growls if you come close.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That’s <strong>right</strong>.</p>",
        "post_number": 32,
